#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD9999 expect=violation domain=ADXX
#note "Mirrors rulespec PMDA-AD9999.yaml (the rule's only prior guard). The Define-XML declares class 'ADAM OTHER' for ADXX - the Define-XML v2.1 ADaM class for a dataset that is none of ADSL/BDS/OCCDS - so upper(ds_class('DEFINE')) is outside the three supported structures and the rule fires once. ADXX is deliberately a non-standard ADaM name so the Define channel is the fixture's only moving part; the rule has no Operations and no structure scope (Domains: ALL), so no library mock beyond the mandatory standard declaration is involved. Killing the Define channel yields EXECUTED with zero findings, which is exactly what the violation expectation here would catch."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#define dataset-class ADXX "ADAM OTHER"
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt define_dataset_class="ADAM OTHER"
dataset ADXX label="Unsupported Analysis Dataset"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | 001
